<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Held at the 2.x line, which is Apache-2.0. From 3.0 ImageSharp is under the Six Labors Split
      License and from 4.0 the package fails the build without a licence key: its targets file runs
      ValidateLicenseTask with ContinueOnError set to Configuration.StartsWith('Debug'), so a key is
      a warning in Debug and an error in Release — and Release is what src/Dockerfile publishes. A
      bump therefore stops every container image building until a key is bought and threaded through
      the image build, which is a purchasing decision rather than a code one.

      Three advisories are open against every version up to 4.1.1, patched only in 4.1.2: the TIFF
      CCITT T4 and T6 *encoders* overrun their output buffers, and HistogramEqualization indexes a
      histogram with an unvalidated luminance. None is reachable from here. This project decodes
      JPEG and PNG, resizes, reads pixels, and encodes PNG and nothing else — see PerspectiveCropper
      SaveAsPng, the only encode in the repository. No TIFF is ever written and no histogram
      processor is ever invoked, so the vulnerable code is not merely unlikely to run but absent
      from the call graph.

      When a licence is in hand: raise this to 4.1.2, set SixLaborsLicenseKey (or drop a sixlabors.lic
      beside the solution), and re-run tools/Enfolderer.Ai.Imaging.TrainingCheck. Expect it to need
      attention — on 4.1.2 it finds 46 of 47 training cards rather than 47, because the rewritten
      JPEG decoder shifts pixels enough to lose one marginal card, and CardArrangementOptions.MinEdge
      sits at a sharp optimum at 1.0 (0.8 through 1.05 were all measured worse).
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="SixLabors.ImageSharp" Version="2.1.11" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Enfolderer.Ai.Contracts\Enfolderer.Ai.Contracts.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
